  "base_rate_reasoning": "This metric is a stock-average rate on a very large debt portfolio, so it changes slowly relative to market rates. In the 2015-2024 sample, annual changes were usually within about plus or minus 0.5 percentage points, with one exceptional +0.90 point catch-up year. Starting from 3.32% at FY2024, a two-year horizon would normally imply only a modest move unless market rates had shifted dramatically for an extended period. The prompt's quoted CBO baseline around 3.3%-3.4% for nearby years is a useful anchor. Balancing that against some residual upward repricing pressure visible in the recent history yields a central estimate slightly above the CBO anchor.",
