    "text": "- 2024-09-30 — Treasury’s **Historical Debt Outstanding** dataset currently shows coverage through **2024-09-30** and is the closest fiscal-year-end debt dataset on Fiscal Data; it states the dataset covers the federal government’s debt outstanding and that the federal fiscal year runs from October 1 to September 30. Source: https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/datasets/historical-debt-outstanding/ ([fiscaldata.treasury.gov](https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/datasets/historical-debt-outstanding/?utm_source=openai))\n- 2025-06-30 — Treasury’s **Treasury Securities Auctions Data** dataset currently shows coverage through **2025-06-30**; it contains auction results used to determine securities’ rates/yields, but it is not a fiscal-year-end total-interest-bearing-debt snapshot. Source: https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/datasets/treasury-securities-auctions-data/ ([fiscaldata.treasury.gov](https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/datasets/treasury-securities-auctions-data/?utm_source=openai))\n- 2025-05-31 — Treasury’s **Monthly Statement of the Public Debt** dataset currently shows coverage through **2025-05-31** and includes Treasury securities outstanding and debt-held-by-the-public tables. Source: https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/datasets/monthly-statement-public-debt/ ([fiscaldata.treasury.gov](https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/datasets/monthly-statement-public-debt/?utm_source=openai))\n- 2025-07-31 — Treasury’s **Schedules of Federal Debt** monthly PDF for **July 2025** reports **Total Federal Debt Held by the Public: $29,531,341** and notes the **average interest rate on Intragovernmental Debt Holdings without TIPS and FRNs for July 31, 2025 was 3.1%**. Source: https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/static-data/published-reports/schedules-fed-debt-monthly/SchedulesFederalDebt_Monthly_202507.pdf ([fiscaldata.treasury.gov](https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/static-data/published-reports/schedules-fed-debt-monthly/SchedulesFederalDebt_Monthly_202507.pdf?utm_source=openai))\n- 2025-05-31 — Treasury’s **Schedules of Federal Debt** monthly PDF for **May 2025** reports the **average interest rate on Intragovernmental Debt Holdings without TIPS and FRNs for May 31, 2025 was 2.9%**. Source: https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/static-data/published-reports/schedules-fed-debt-monthly/SchedulesFederalDebt_Monthly_202505.pdf ([fiscaldata.treasury.gov](https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/static-data/published-reports/schedules-fed-debt-monthly/SchedulesFederalDebt_Monthly_202505.pdf?utm_source=openai))\n\nI did **not** find a Fiscal Data source matching **2026-09-30** itself; the newest official Fiscal Data results I found were through 2025, so a 2026-09-30 figure is not available from the sources returned here. ([fiscaldata.treasury.gov](https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/datasets/historical-debt-outstanding/?utm_source=openai))"
   },
   {
    "provider": "web_search",
    "url": null,
    "title": "Fiscal Data Average Interest Rate Amount Interest-bearing Debt Total Interest-bearing Debt Sep 2026",
    "published": null,
    "text": "- 2025-01-31 — Treasury’s Monthly Statement of the Public Debt dataset says it is published on the fourth business day of each month and details debt as of the end of the previous month; the dataset includes the “Average Interest Rate,” “Amount,” and “Total Interest-bearing Debt” concepts you asked about. Source: https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/datasets/monthly-statement-public-debt/ ([fiscaldata.treasury.gov](https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/datasets/monthly-statement-public-debt/?utm_source=openai))\n- 2025-02-28 — The Treasury’s published MSPD PDF for February 2025 includes a table with the columns “Average Interest Rate” and “Amount,” and a “Total Interest-bearing Debt” line item. Source: https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/static-data/published-reports/mspd-entire/MonthlyStatementPublicDebt_Entire_202502.pdf ([fiscaldata.treasury.gov](https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/static-data/published-reports/mspd-entire/MonthlyStatementPublicDebt_Entire_202502.pdf?utm_source=openai))\n- 2025-01-31 — The Treasury’s published MSPD PDF for January 2025 also includes “Average Interest Rate,” “Amount,” and “Total Interest-bearing Debt” in its summary table. Source: https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/static-data/published-reports/mspd-entire/MonthlyStatementPublicDebt_Entire_202501.pdf ([fiscaldata.treasury.gov](https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/static-data/published-reports/mspd-entire/MonthlyStatementPublicDebt_Entire_202501.pdf?utm_source=openai))\n- 2025-09-30 — Treasury Fiscal Data’s Historical Debt Outstanding dataset currently shows data through the end of fiscal year 2024, with new data expected in 2025; this is the closest official Fiscal Data dataset page I found for end-of-fiscal-year debt totals, but it does not yet show September 2026 figures. Source: https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/datasets/historical-debt-outstanding/ ([fiscaldata.treasury.gov](https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/datasets/historical-debt-outstanding/?utm_source=openai))\n\nI could not verify any official Fiscal Data publication for **September 2026** yet, because that date is in the future relative to the available Treasury sources I found. If you want, I can keep searching specific Treasury PDF releases or the Fiscal Data API once September 2026 data exists."
   },
   {
    "provider": "web_search",
    "url": null,
    "title": "site:fiscaldata.treasury.gov/datasets/average-interest-rates-treasury-securities 2026 total interest-bearing debt",
    "published": null,
    "text": "- 2025-05-31 — Treasury’s Monthly Statement / Schedules of Federal Debt show **Federal Debt Held by the Public** at **$28,952,461 million**; this is the most recent relevant published monthly figure I found in the Treasury Fiscal Data materials returned by the search. ([fiscaldata.treasury.gov](https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/static-data/published-reports/schedules-fed-debt-monthly/SchedulesFederalDebt_Monthly_202505.pdf?utm_source=openai)) — https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/static-data/published-reports/schedules-fed-debt-monthly/SchedulesFederalDebt_Monthly_202505.pdf\n\n- 2025-05-31 — In the same Treasury schedule, **nonmarketable securities** were **$383,184 million** and **total marketable securities** were **$28,569,277 million**, which together reconcile to the public-debt total above. ([fiscaldata.treasury.gov](https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/static-data/published-reports/schedules-fed-debt-monthly/SchedulesFederalDebt_Monthly_202505.pdf?utm_source=openai)) — https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/static-data/published-reports/schedules-fed-debt-monthly/SchedulesFederalDebt_Monthly_202505.pdf\n\n- 2025-05-31 — Treasury’s note says the **average interest rate on Intragovernmental Debt Holdings without TIPS and FRNs** was **2.9%** as of this date. ([fiscaldata.treasury.gov](https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/static-data/published-reports/schedules-fed-debt-monthly/SchedulesFederalDebt_Monthly_202505.pdf?utm_source=openai)) — https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/static-data/published-reports/schedules-fed-debt-monthly/SchedulesFederalDebt_Monthly_202505.pdf\n\n- 2025-06-30 — The next monthly Treasury schedule available in search results reports **Federal Debt Held by the Public principal** at **$28,307,312 million** and **Intragovernmental Debt Holdings principal** at **$7,152,848 million**. ([fiscaldata.treasury.gov](https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/static-data/published-reports/schedules-fed-debt-monthly/SchedulesFederalDebt_Monthly_202506.pdf?utm_source=openai)) — https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/static-data/published-reports/schedules-fed-debt-monthly/SchedulesFederalDebt_Monthly_202506.pdf\n\n- 2025-07-31 — Treasury’s July schedule reports **total interest expense on federal debt managed by Fiscal Service** of **$1,011,127 million** and notes that the **average interest rate on Intragovernmental Debt Holdings without TIPS and FRNs** was **3.1%**. ([fiscaldata.treasury.gov](https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/static-data/published-reports/schedules-fed-debt-monthly/SchedulesFederalDebt_Monthly_202507.pdf?utm_source=openai)) — https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/static-data/published-reports/schedules-fed-debt-monthly/SchedulesFederalDebt_Monthly_202507.pdf\n\nNote: I did not find a direct 2026 result for the exact query phrase “total interest-bearing debt” on the specified Fiscal Data dataset page; the most relevant official Treasury results available in the search results were the monthly Schedules of Federal Debt and related debt datasets."
