    "title": "US Treasury fiscal data average interest rates on U.S. Treasury securities September 2026",
    "published": null,
    "text": "- 2026-09-10 — U.S. Treasury’s daily yield curve page shows the latest available row on that page as **2026-09-10**, with constant-maturity Treasury yields including **1-month 3.91%**, **3-month 4.00%**, **2-year 4.63%**, **10-year 4.84%**, **20-year 4.95%**, and **30-year 5.37%**. Source: https://home.treasury.gov/resource-center/data-chart-center/interest-rates/TextView?field_tdr_date_value=2026&type=daily_treasury_yield_curve ([home.treasury.gov](https://home.treasury.gov/resource-center/data-chart-center/interest-rates/TextView?field_tdr_date_value=2026&type=daily_treasury_yield_curve))\n\n- 2026-09-09 — Treasury’s daily real yield curve page shows the latest available row on that page as **2026-09-09**, with real yields including **5-year 2.98%** and **10-year 3.95%** on that date. Source: https://home.treasury.gov/resource-center/data-chart-center/interest-rates/TextView?field_tdr_date_value=2026&type=daily_treasury_real_yield_curve ([home.treasury.gov](https://home.treasury.gov/resource-center/data-chart-center/interest-rates/TextView?field_tdr_date_value=2026&type=daily_treasury_real_yield_curve&utm_source=openai))\n\n- 2026-09-09 — Treasury’s daily bill-rate page shows the latest available row on that page as **2026-09-09**; it is the official Treasury source for daily secondary-market quotations on Treasury bills. Source: https://home.treasury.gov/resource-center/data-chart-center/interest-rates/TextView?field_tdr_date_value=2026&type=daily_treasury_bill_rates ([home.treasury.gov](https://home.treasury.gov/resource-center/data-chart-center/interest-rates/TextView?field_tdr_date_value_month=202609&type=daily_treasury_bill_rates&utm_source=openai))\n\n- 2025-07-31 — In Treasury’s monthly **Schedules of Federal Debt** publication, the **average interest rate on Treasury bills** was **4.3%**, Treasury notes **3.1%**, Treasury bonds **3.3%**, TIPS **0.9%**, and Treasury Floating Rate Notes **4.4%**. Source: https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/static-data/published-reports/schedules-fed-debt-monthly/SchedulesFederalDebt_Monthly_202507.pdf ([fiscaldata.treasury.gov](https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/static-data/published-reports/schedules-fed-debt-monthly/SchedulesFederalDebt_Monthly_202507.pdf?utm_source=openai))\n\n- 2025-07-31 — In the same Treasury debt schedule, the **average interest rate on federal debt held by the public** was **3.8%** including nonmarketable securities, and **3.1%** for intragovernmental debt holdings excluding TIPS and FRNs. Source: https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/static-data/published-reports/schedules-fed-debt-monthly/SchedulesFederalDebt_Monthly_202507.pdf ([fiscaldata.treasury.gov](https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/static-data/published-reports/schedules-fed-debt-monthly/SchedulesFederalDebt_Monthly_202507.pdf?utm_source=openai))\n\n- 2025-07-31 — Treasury’s debt schedule notes that the **TIPS Federal Debt Held by the Public inflation-adjusted principal balance includes inflation of $367,293 million** as of that date. Source: https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/static-data/published-reports/schedules-fed-debt-monthly/SchedulesFederalDebt_Monthly_202507.pdf ([fiscaldata.treasury.gov](https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/static-data/published-reports/schedules-fed-debt-monthly/SchedulesFederalDebt_Monthly_202507.pdf?utm_source=openai))\n\n- 2026-09-30 — I did **not** find an official Treasury/Fiscal Data monthly schedule for September 2026 in the web results available to me, so I could not verify September 2026 monthly average-interest-rate figures from the debt schedule itself. Source: search results from Fiscal Data/Treasury only; no September 2026 monthly PDF located. ([fiscaldata.treasury.gov](https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/static-data/published-reports/schedules-fed-debt-monthly/SchedulesFederalDebt_Monthly_202507.pdf?utm_source=openai))\n\n"
   },
